WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:23.820
OK?

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.480
I really need everybody to understand this
because this is so important.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:33.320
The strategy by Donald Trump of saying that
the election will be unfair and rigged is

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.710
working.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.850
If it wasn't convincing anybody, we could
ignore it.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.720
It might be no big deal, but it is working.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:48.290
Donald Trump has convinced 65 percent of Republican
voters that the upcoming election might not

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.550
be fair.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:56.790
This is a poll based on more than 44000 U.S.
adults with a one percent margin of error.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.030
Now, here's what makes this really tricky.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.800
Sixty five percent of Republicans questioned
whether the election will be fair.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.950
Forty six percent of Democrats also aren't
confident that the election will be fair.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.170
But the devil is in the details because the
concerns about fairness from Republicans are

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.220
very different than the concerns about fairness
from the Democrats.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.920
And it really comes down to understanding
these details.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.990
Republicans who think the election might not
be fair are falling for what Donald Trump

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:28.369
has been saying, which is mail in ballots
will be riddled with fraud.

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:30.830
We won't know the election results for a long
time.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.830
They are rigging it.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.650
That's what the Republican voters have fallen
for.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:40.680
Democrats, on the other hand, are worried
that Trump is making the election not fair.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:46.130
By breaking the post office, by filing lawsuits,
by trying to suppress the vote, so on and

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:51.550
so forth, preventing vote by mail, purging
voter rolls, doing all of the things that

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:55.410
Republicans have been doing for decades to
try to win elections by suppressing the vote.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.180
So these are not asymmetrical concerns.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.530
If you glance at the numbers and you say,
OK, well, it seems like Republicans or Democrats

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:07.370
and Democrats are basically in agreement just
to slightly different degrees.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.700
Forty six percent of Dems think the election
might be unfair.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.669
Sixty five percent of Republicans, no big
deal, slight party difference.

00:02:14.669 --> 00:02:19.900
The reasons why they think there might not
be fairness are what is so dramatically different.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.590
And what you have to understand in order to
really synthesize this properly is the history

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.519
of voter suppression historically.

00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:31.769
Democrats try to increase voter turnout, period.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:35.569
They just say if more people vote, we're better
off in general.

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:41.139
Republicans have employed a strategy of trying
to limit voter turnout in very particular

00:02:41.139 --> 00:02:42.709
and specific ways.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:50.169
Polling shows that it's Trump who will most
likely or more likely need foul play in order

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.169
to win.

00:02:51.169 --> 00:02:53.230
Democrats simply want the election to happen.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.129
They want everybody who wants to vote to get
to vote, and they want every single one of

00:02:57.129 --> 00:02:58.810
those votes to be counted.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.829
And it's true.

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:01.730
If that happens, it's better for Joe Biden.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:02.730
We know that.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:09.319
To be true, the president is the one who realizes
that he might need voter fraud and voter suppression

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:10.359
to win.

00:03:10.359 --> 00:03:15.560
As I told you in the last segment, and the
scariest thing is that it's working for Donald

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:21.159
Trump, are concerned for a long time, has
been if it's close in November.

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:27.439
And Trump claims it was rigged and it activates
his followers, many with their guns, to hit

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:28.439
the streets.

00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:30.930
That could get very ugly and it could happen
very quickly.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.049
It could happen within hours of whenever Trump
claims the rigging took place.

00:03:35.049 --> 00:03:41.569
So when we hear that there are no gaps in
the confidence people have in our voting systems,

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:47.629
we can't forget that one side is the side
that tries to lower turnout in order to win,

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:52.769
meaning a ton of Trump ists are happy that
the election might not be fair.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:55.589
This has always been the point of attacking
it.

00:03:55.589 --> 00:03:58.779
And this is why it will continue unless we
stop it.

00:03:58.779 --> 00:03:59.779
This is how it starts.

00:03:59.779 --> 00:04:04.590
This is how you weaponize people to hit the
streets, maybe with guns to demand that you

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.809
be kept in power.

00:04:05.809 --> 00:04:08.479
These are not inconsequential or trivial matters.

00:04:08.479 --> 00:04:10.579
Now, what can we do?

00:04:10.579 --> 00:04:15.510
If you want to find out how and where you
can vote early, check out the page called

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.310
Early Voting by State on Vote Dawg.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.940
We're linking to that page in the description
to the YouTube video for this story.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.120
And you will very quickly see that every state
is different here in Massachusetts, for example.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.030
Early voting starts 11 days before this is
in-person.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.650
Early voting starts 11 days before the election.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:38.120
In Michigan, it starts 45 days before the
election.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.500
We're getting close to that in Florida.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.860
It's early voting starts at least 10 days
before the election.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:46.860
If not earlier.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.330
So understand that.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:53.190
Understand what the rules are for voting absentee
in your state.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:59.949
You probably in most states, you probably
already can request an absentee ballot.

00:04:59.949 --> 00:05:00.949
I've already done it.

00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:04.569
I've received my primary ballot for the September
1st election.

00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:09.310
And sometime after September 1st, I'm going
to be receiving my absentee ballot for the

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.280
general election in November.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.290
Understand all of these things.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.750
Figure out how you plan to vote.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.510
And then let's activate whoever we can and
make sure that people that are already on

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.259
our side plan to vote.

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:23.210
Particularly when, you know, Trump wants to
make it difficult to vote.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.270
But the reality is, in most states, it's actually
easier than ever to vote.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.689
With early voting, with expanded absentee
ballot access, there's no excuse for not voting

00:05:31.689 --> 00:05:34.129
this time around in many people.

00:05:34.129 --> 00:05:35.490
Metaphorically.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:40.759
This time around are willing to crawl over
broken glass in over two in order to vote.

00:05:40.759 --> 00:05:41.759
Some would literally do it.

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:41.960
I'm using it metaphorically.

